---
export const prerender = false;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const h2s = "font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:200;font-size:1.125rem;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--parchment);margin-bottom:0.75rem;";
const st  = "color:var(--parchment);font-weight:500;";
const ul  = "padding-left:1.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.5rem;";
const lk  = "color:var(--amber);";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How (K)Need collects, uses and protects your personal information.">
  <main class="wf-container py-page" style="max-width:46rem;">
    <div class="wf-page-head">
      <div class="wf-eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="wf-page-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="wf-page-intro">Last updated 1 September 2026. This policy applies to kneed.tv and all related services.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="simple-body">

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Who We Are</h2>
        <p>(K)Need is a digital journal about Melbourne's neighbourhood bakeries, produced by Comma Films Pty Ltd, based in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia. We operate the website at kneed.tv ("the Site"). In this policy, "we", "us" and "our" refers to Comma Films Pty Ltd.</p>
        <p>For any privacy enquiries, contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@kneed.tv" style={lk}>hello@kneed.tv</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>What We Collect</h2>

        <p><strong style={st}>Account and profile.</strong> Your email address, and if you sign in with Google, your name and profile photo. You may add a display name, username and bio. Your display name appears next to any comments you post; nothing else in your profile is shown publicly.</p>

        <p><strong style={st}>Optional demographic data.</strong> With your explicit consent only: your date of birth, gender, and suburb or location, used solely for anonymous, aggregate analytics. You can withdraw consent at any time via the Edit Profile page, which deletes the data immediately and records a timestamp of the change.</p>

        <p><strong style={st}>Activity.</strong> Comments, ratings and saved bakeries, linked to your account.</p>

        <p><strong style={st}>Bakery submissions.</strong> What you enter in the form: bakery name, address, suburb, website, Instagram handle, notes and your name, with email address and phone number optional. We also record the IP address of the request for spam prevention. Submissions are visible to site admins only.</p>

        <p><strong style={st}>Newsletter.</strong> Your email address, the source and timestamp of your consent, and the IP address of the request for spam prevention. Every email we send includes an unsubscribe link.</p>

        <p><strong style={st}>Usage and device data (consent-gated).</strong> If you click Accept on the consent banner, our analytics and advertising tools collect pages visited, session duration, approximate geographic location, device and browser information, and on-page interactions such as button clicks and form use. Nothing loads if you decline.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>How We Use Your Data</h2>
        <p>To operate your account and its features; to publish your comments and ratings; to review bakery submissions; to send the email you have asked for; to produce anonymous, aggregate analytics that shape our editorial focus; and to meet our legal obligations.</p>
        <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for automated decision-making or profiling that produces legal or similarly significant effects.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Google Sign-In Data</h2>
        <p>If you sign in with Google, we receive your email address, name and profile photo from Google. We use them only to create and operate your account on the Site. We store them in our database, we do not disclose them to anyone other than the service providers described below, and we never use them for advertising.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Who We Share Data With</h2>
        <p>We use third-party service providers to run the Site, and share personal information with them only as far as needed for that purpose. As at the date at the top of this page, they fall into these categories:</p>
        <ul style="padding-left:1.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem;">
          <li><strong style={st}>Database, authentication and hosting.</strong> Your account, profile, comments, ratings and submissions are stored with our database and hosting providers, currently Supabase and Cloudflare.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Email delivery.</strong> Your email address is passed to our email provider, currently Resend, to send the messages you have signed up for or requested.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Analytics and advertising.</strong> Only if you consent, usage and device data is sent to Google via Google Analytics and to Meta via the Meta Pixel. Meta may combine it with data it already holds about you. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style={lk}>Google's Privacy Policy</a>, the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style={lk}>Google Analytics opt-out tool</a>, <a href="https://www.meta.com/en-gb/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style={lk}>Meta's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://accountscenter.facebook.com/ad_preferences" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style={lk}>Meta ad settings</a>.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Content delivery and embedded media.</strong> Pages load fonts, images, map tiles and video embeds from third-party services, which receive your IP address as part of serving them. Playing an embedded video also sends viewing data to the video host.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Address autocomplete.</strong> Text you type into the address and suburb fields on the submission form and the profile edit page is sent to Google's Places API.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This list reflects our current providers and may change as we change tools. We may also disclose personal information if required to do so by law, or to protect the rights, property or safety of (K)Need, our users or the public.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Overseas Storage</h2>
        <p>Some of these providers store or process data on servers outside Australia, including in the United States.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
        <p>We use your browser's local storage to keep you signed in and to remember your consent choice. If you consent to analytics and advertising, Meta sets a cookie in your browser to identify it for advertising purposes. No analytics or advertising cookies are set if you decline, or before you have made a choice. No other cookies are set by this site.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Analytics and Consent</h2>
        <p>Google Analytics 4 and the Meta Pixel do not load unless you explicitly click <strong style={st}>Accept</strong> on the consent banner shown on your first visit. If you click <strong style={st}>Decline</strong>, neither tracker loads and nothing is sent to Google or Meta from your visit. Your choice persists across future visits.</p>
        <p>You can change your choice at any time using the <strong style={st}>Privacy choices</strong> link in the site footer, which clears your saved choice and re-displays the banner. Neither tracker loads on the sign-in callback page, even with consent granted.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>How We Keep Your Data Safe</h2>
        <p>We take reasonable steps to protect your information, including access controls and encryption of data in transit. No online service can be completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Data Retention</h2>
        <ul style={ul}>
          <li><strong style={st}>Account and profile:</strong> kept while your account is active. If you ask us to delete it, we do so within 30 days of your request.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Comments, ratings and saved bakeries:</strong> deleted or de-identified when your account is deleted.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Demographic data:</strong> deleted immediately when you withdraw consent via the Edit Profile page.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Bakery submissions:</strong> kept while they remain relevant to the Site. The IP address recorded for spam prevention is kept only as long as needed for that purpose.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Newsletter:</strong> kept until you unsubscribe. After you unsubscribe, we keep a minimal suppression record so that we do not contact you again.</li>
          <li><strong style={st}>Analytics:</strong> retained for up to 14 months.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Children</h2>
        <p>The Site is intended for a general adult audience and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Your Rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask us to access or correct the personal information we hold about you, delete your account and associated personal data, or withdraw consent for demographic data collection at any time via your profile settings. Email us at <a href="mailto:hello@kneed.tv" style={lk}>hello@kneed.tv</a> and we will respond within 30 days.</p>
        <p>If you believe your privacy rights have been breached, you can complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC).</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will update the "last updated" date at the top of this page.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 style={h2s}>Contact</h2>
        <p>For any privacy questions or requests, please contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@kneed.tv" style={lk}>hello@kneed.tv</a>.</p>
        <p>Comma Films Pty Ltd<br/>Melbourne, Victoria, Australia</p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
